_🚀 Performance & Scalability_ | _🔵 Trivial_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**`oneDoor()` re-reads every file once per fact instead of once total.**

`files.filter((f) => rx.test(fs.readFileSync(f, 'utf8')))` runs inside the `for (const [fact, rx] of Object.entries(FACTS))` loop (8 facts), so every matching `.js` file under `src` is read from disk 8 times instead of once. For a "full-estate sweep" meant to run across the whole repo, this is an easily-avoided 8x I/O multiplier.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-  for (const [fact, rx] of Object.entries(FACTS)) {
-    const producers = files.filter((f) => rx.test(fs.readFileSync(f, 'utf8'))).map((f) => f.replace(ROOT + '/', ''));
+  const contents = new Map(files.map((f) => [f, fs.readFileSync(f, 'utf8')]));
+  for (const [fact, rx] of Object.entries(FACTS)) {
+    const producers = files.filter((f) => rx.test(contents.get(f))).map((f) => f.replace(ROOT + '/', ''));
```
</details>

