_🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🔴 Critical_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**`_SM`/`_manifest` are out of scope here — this throws on every build, and the manifest is sealed before `llm_verify` is known anyway.**

Two compounding defects:

1. **ReferenceError**: `_SM` and `_manifest` are `const`-declared inside `buildPayload()` (lines 250-251), a *sibling* function to `build()`, not a closure over it. Neither identifier exists in `build()`'s scope, so this line throws `ReferenceError` on every single call — uncaught, since nothing wraps it in try/catch. Every audit mint would crash here.
2. **Sealed too early**: even granting scope access, `_SM.seal(_manifest)` already ran at line 858, inside `buildPayload()`, before `llm_verify` — a REQUIRED stage — is ever recorded. `seal()` snapshots `sendable`/`missing_required`/`complete` at call time; mutating `stages.llm_verify` afterwards doesn't recompute them. Since `llm_verify` is always `not_reached` at seal time, `payload.stage_manifest.sendable` would be permanently `false` for every audit, defeating the manifest's purpose entirely.

Fix by operating on the already-sealed `payload.stage_manifest` object (same underlying reference) and re-sealing after the update.




<details>
<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
   payload.llm_verify = _llmv;
-  if (_llmv && _llmv.status && _llmv.status !== 'unavailable') _SM.ran(_manifest, 'llm_verify');
-  else _SM.failed(_manifest, 'llm_verify', (_llmv && _llmv.error) || 'verifier unavailable');
+  {
+    const _SM = require(path.resolve(ROOT, 'src', 'lib', 'audit', 'stage-manifest.js'));
+    if (_llmv && _llmv.status && _llmv.status !== 'unavailable') _SM.ran(payload.stage_manifest, 'llm_verify');
+    else _SM.failed(payload.stage_manifest, 'llm_verify', (_llmv && _llmv.error) || 'verifier unavailable');
+    payload.stage_manifest = _SM.seal(payload.stage_manifest);
+  }
```
</details>

